        (63, null, '[]', 'Dear Nguyen Pham Thu Ha,


Thanks for joining the course! I look forward to working with you to help 
you get ready for your university studies!


In this course, Problem-Solving Skills for University Success, you’ll learn 
the skills to help you excel at university, such as understanding the 
different kinds of problems you may encounter at university, strategies for 
understanding a problem, working with others and using creative ideation 
techniques to identify solutions to problems, as well as skills for 
evaluating and presenting solutions to those problems. All these things and 
more will be covered in this course, preparing you for your university 
experience.


The course is made up of five modules with 4 lessons in each. Each lesson 
consists of lectures and interviews with experts in their fields and in 
academic culture. There are also practice quizzes to help you apply the 
course content, and discussion boards so that you can relate course 
concepts to your own experiences and discuss them with your peers. There is 
also an additional sixth module for the final summative assignment where 
you can apply the skills and knowledge gained from the course to a more 
substantial assignment. To pass the course, you’ll need to pass the 
summative assignment, successfully complete the summative quizzes in each 
module, and take part in the discussion boards.


If you have any friends starting university soon, feel free to forward them 
this email about the course. Once again I’d like to welcome you to the 
course, and I look forward to working with you over the next 6 weeks!


Kind regards,


Lydia Dutcher


Problem-Solving Skills for University Success MOOC Instructor


P.S. Don’t forget to keep an eye out for the special links ;-)


