        (91, null, '[]', 'Dear Nguyen Pham Thu Ha,


Congratulations on finishing the Academic Skills for University Success 
Specialization! Well done on all your hard work and active participation on 
each of the five different courses! Whether you decided to take on our 
Specialization to learn something new before starting or continuing your 
undergraduate studies, in order to brush up on your academic skills or just 
because, we hope you have enjoyed this Specialization and have learnt some 
valuable skills along the way!


The skills you’ve developed in the Advanced Skills for University Success 
Specialization will help you get a head start in your university studies, 
and equip you with the tools you need to excel in the competitive 
university environment. You’ve developed skills essential to academic 
success – Communication, Information and Digital Literacy, Critical 
Thinking & Problem Solving – and put these into action through practical 
tasks. In the Capstone Project, you applied the academic knowledge and 
skills you learnt throughout courses 1-4 to research, write and present 
project proposal that addressed a complex, real-world problem related to 
your field of interest and/or future study.


This course requires a lot of time, thought and mental energy: finishing it 
deserves a reward, so we hope you take some time out and spoil yourself. 
You deserve it!


Coursera will be in contact with details on how to download your 
certificate.


If you haven’t already, tell us what you thought of the course in the 
discussion forums, or write your own Learner Story!


Kind regards, and good luck for the future,


Jessica Blackburn


