        (104, null, '[]', 'Hello Nguyễn Phạm Thu,

Get ready for a transformative educational experience coming July 2024 at Cisco Networking Academy! We''re integrating cutting-edge AI, gamification, and adaptive learning into our platforms for a dynamic, 
personalized, unified learning environment for you.

There are many ways to get involved this year outside of taking courses. Learn how we celebrated International Day of Education on January 24 (and jump in!). Join us for Backstage with the Dream Team at our next Women Rock-IT event on February 29. Additionally, you can learn from women in AI at International Girls in ICT Day on April 25.
Platform Updates
Password change coming
Starting February 24, you may be prompted to change your password (which will be used on both platforms). You have until July to make the change, when the two platforms will converge.
Keep your learning history
Do you have both a NetAcad and a SkillsForAll account? Take action by February 22 to maintain your learning history.
Cool new course features
Lots of exciting functionality is now available on Skills for All, including Class Messaging which uses the power of Webex messaging.
Learning Updates
What is IoT and the jobs it creates?
Learn about great job opportunities for professionals with IoT skills and start building your own skills today. Now in 10 languages.
Learn JavaScript and get certified
From interactive websites to dynamic web applications, JavaScript is the driving force behind 
user-friendly interfaces.
New in Professional Skills
Employers seek well-rounded candidates. These courses complement your IT training with interpersonal skills for workplace success.
New in Entrepreneurship
Managing a Business Venture, the final course in a 3-part entrepreneurship series, is coming soon on 
Skills for All as self-paced and instructor-led.
Get Excited, Get Involved
Backstage with the Dream Team
At the next Women Rock-IT on February 29, hear the Dream Team share their experience working at a global event with Cisco. Registration opens February 1.
#AreYouAiReady ?
Save the date for Girls in ICT Day on April 25. Learn from women leading the way in artificial intelligence.
