        (155, null, '[]', 'Hello Nguyen Pham Thu Ha,


Thank you for enrolling in Introduction to HTML5. In this course we look 
into the basic concepts of HTML5 - the language used to create the content 
for webpages. We learn more than just the language though, we also look at 
how the World Wide Web evolved from a place for Physics researchers geek 
out over technical physics articles to an ever-changing place for 
information, entertainment, and communication. When you complete the 
course, you will come away with an understanding of how the web works, what 
web developers need to consider when designing accessible web sites, and 
how easy it actually is to create a webpage.


We would like to find out a bit more about your interest in this course as 
well as your educational background. This information will help improve 
this course and other online courses offered by the University of Michigan. 
The survey will only take about 5-10 minutes to complete.


Click here to take the survey.
<https://eventing.coursera.-.-TbelX4rwIilEhdENnsjuUo0OwHHLEkZQs7Ddg9yjZk>


How will you know if this course is right for you? Well, not every course 
can cater to every student. This one is NOT for experienced programmers. 
But if you have ever wondered what happens when you type an address into 
the URL bar at the top of your browser, you will find out. If you have ever 
been a little nervous about asking what something means or how something 
works, I also hope this will be the community for you. Because that is what 
I want to turn this course into; a community of learners who are just 
starting out but who want to learn a little bit more. So whether you join 
me for just this class, or for all the upcoming Web Design for Everybody 
Specialization courses, I welcome you.


Colleen


