Products Page Improvement

Monday 19th August


 
 Dear User,


We are writing to inform you about an initiative that aims to enhance the customer experience by making improvements to the Pearson English Portal products page. This includes addressing pain points identified through internal and customer research and implementing new design features such as:


1. ''Add a Product'' button at the top, and not at the bottom.
Benefit: Accelerate product setup.

2. Separate tabs for Pearson English Connect, MyEnglishLab and Test Hub on the menu bar.
Benefit: Quicker access to these platforms without having to look for the product first.

3. Additional Product - Level - Component filter. 

Benefit: Find the searched component more quickly.

4. New position of the ''Class schedule'' button. The ''Class schedule'' button has been moved to the ''Classes'' page.
Benefit: Reduce confusion for non-Pearson English Portal users.

5. New position of the information on the number of components. The information on the number of components is now shown in the ''Product Level'' container, and not in the ''Product Title'' container.
Benefit: The information is now more accurate.


We hope you enjoy these features. Our aim is to bring you the best possible experience when using Pearson English Portal.


 
Kind regards,

Pearson English Language Learning (ELL)

