[MongoDB Go Driver 1.17.1 Released][3]

 The MongoDB Go Driver Team is pleased to release version 1.17.1 of the official Go driver. 
Release Notes
This release improves the behavior of connection checkout by checking for closed connections. 
It also fixes a bug where the authSource from a TXT record would be overridden for auth mechanisms 
that require an authSource of $external. 

For a full list of tickets included in this release, please see the links below: 

Improvements
Bugs
Tasks

Full Changelog: v1.17.0…v1.17.1 
Documentation for the Go driver can be found on pkg.go.dev and the MongoDB documentation site. BSON library documentation is also available on pkg.go.dev. Questions and inquiries can be asked on the MongoDB Developer Community. Bugs can be reported in the Go Driver project in the MongoDB JIRA where a list of current issues can be found. Your feedback on the Go driver is greatly appreciated!
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------


[MongoDB 8.0.0 is released][4]

 MongoDB 8.0 is now available for download! There are 4 major areas of improvement in MongoDB 8.0 including: 

Up to 36% higher throughput compared with the previous version
Easier and cheaper to get started with horizontal scaling
Expanded use cases for working with encrypted data
Additional controls to help ensure healthy behavior during periods of heavy load

MongoDB 8.0 is available today via MongoDB Atlas, as part of MongoDB Enterprise Advanced for on-premises and hybrid deployments, and as a free download from mongodb.com/try. 
You can also review the release notes to learn more about the new features as well as the upgrade procedures. 
We would also like to thank the following community members who have contributed to this release: 
Tedi Roca, y yz, Roey Maor, Mika Fischer, Joseph Ferguson, Yi-Jyun Pan, Daniel Jewell, Wernfried Domscheit, Chan Lewis, dongyu si, Jun Jin, Łukasz Gębicki, Yongheng Chen, Bouke Haarsma, Aleksandr Nechaev, Ian Springer, Sven Varkel, Yazhou Yang 
