        (266, null, '[]', 'Welcome to Java Basics!


Here are a few things you should know about this course:


1. Powered by Codio


This course is powered by Codio - meaning you will see a fully operational 
code editor in your browser tab without installing anything. This enables a 
truly hands-on experience from Day 1!


2. Less Text (and no video) approach


Codio presents the material in smaller lessons that are more manageable. 
The same vocabulary and concepts are covered, but in a more approachable 
way — stating things as plainly as possible, and, when appropriate, using 
images, tables, or lists.


Research shows this now only increases the amount of content remembered, 
raises learner satisfaction, increases learner understanding for non-native 
English speakers, and doubles learning gains -- but most importantly it 
saves you time!


3. Instant feedback on every page


Every page of content in Codio ends with an assessment - giving you an 
instant check on your understanding before you move on. Throughout each 
module, assessments progress from quick checks such as multiple choice and 
fill-in-the-blank to longer programming assessments which check the code 
you have written.


4. Many Small Programs for assessment


The last lesson on every module is Coding Exercises where you are asked to 
write 5 short programs. Each one should take you minutes, making them more 
approachable and offering you feedback more often than large projects 
frequently found in CS courses. You need to get 4 out of 5 correct to pass 
the lesson. If you ever want to retry, no worries! Follow the direction in 
the "How to Reset a Graded Assignment in Codio" Reading assignment or 
simply email the course name and assignment name to help@codio.com from 
this email address and we''ll reset it for you.


Good luck and happy coding!


