        (352, null, '[]', 'Hi Nguyen, 

Gartner predicts 40% of enterprise apps will incorporate AI by the end of this year, so you may find yourself in learning mode. An essential element of AI-powered business apps is vector search. Here’s your chance to learn more about it.

Because more than 80% of information is unstructured, search is moving beyond keywords. Vector embeddings help contextualize all of this data, even when your end users might not know what they’re looking for. 

View this video presentation with MongoDB and Redmonk <https://em.mongodb.com/MTQ5LUNCSi0xMzYAAAGXwde5Z7KeHrZHAw6jPWZMKlAs2zGObJmt4ue42FIsPWfTeHTRK-GbiZUgJGd15tUQcD6U1xo=> to understand:


	- What vector search is
	- What it does
	- Common use cases
	- How MongoDB Atlas stores vector embeddings alongside operational data



PS. Ready to try Atlas Vector Search? Head over to our quick-start guide <https://em.mongodb.com/MTQ5LUNCSi0xMzYAAAGXwde5Zy05Bss03I4dW6xKE1PMx0lr4xLMYQHKRoz-269bHzjVMNQRgn_dQcFY8oB2zioL1KY=> to get started today.
View the presentation <https://em.mongodb.com/MTQ5LUNCSi0xMzYAAAGXwde5Z7KeHrZHAw6jPWZMKlAs2zGObJmt4ue42FIsPWfTeHTRK-GbiZUgJGd15tUQcD6U1xo=>
Cheers, 
 The MongoDB Team
