        (513, null, '[]', 'Two powerful ways to bring structure and consistency to your API workflow 


 
 
<https://community.postman.com/t/the-postman-drop-design-sync-and-manage-apis-without-the-switching-tax/78684?utm_campaign=global_fy26q1_prdctcm_spechub&utm_medium=email&utm_source=db_nl&utm_content=segment4>
 

Hi Thu,



 Designing reliable APIs gets harder as things scale—but now you’ve got better 
ways to stay ahead. With the new types in collections and Spec Hub, Postman 
gives you two paths to bring structure and consistency into your API workflow 
without switching tools or adding complexity.

Here’s how types in collections help:

 * Catch mismatches early with built-in validation
 *  Define data models across requests
 * Enhance docs with clear, structured data models
And with Spec Hub, you can:

 * Work on specs directly—no more import/export juggling
 * Share specs so your team stays in sync
 * Convert specs into Postman Collections with a single click
Whether you prefer starting from a schema or evolving as you build, Postman 
has you covered.

Learn More  
<https://community.postman.com/t/the-postman-drop-design-sync-and-manage-apis-without-the-switching-tax/78684?utm_campaign=global_fy26q1_prdctcm_spechub&utm_medium=email&utm_source=db_nl&utm_content=segment4>
  


