        (540, null, '[]', 'Congratulations on finishing the Introduction to Research for Essay Writing 
course! Now, you know everything you need to know to write a college 
research paper. Good job!


If you have completed all four courses in the Academic English: Writing 
specialization, you are ready to take complete the Capstone Project, in 
which you will write a complete research paper and practice all of the 
skills you have been learning.


If you’re interested in improving your English skills further, we welcome 
you to take another specialization, such as Learn English: Advanced Grammar 
and Punctuation, Academic English: Writing, Learn English: Intermediate 
Grammar, Learn English: Advanced Academic Speaking and Listening, or The 
Pronunciation of American English. Look for all of these on the Coursera 
website.


If you’re interested in furthering your studies, UCI is offers a wide 
variety of online teacher-led courses in English and Teaching English as a 
Second Language, as well as hundreds of courses in business and other 
professional fields. For more information about those, contact us at 
ip@ce.uci.edu.


And if you’re really motivated to learn more, consider coming to the 
University of California, Irvine to study in one of our English language or 
professional certificate programs. You can find information about that on 
our website: https://ip.ce.uci.edu/.


As we try to improve Introduction to Research for Essay Writing—we have an 
end-of-course survey that we would really appreciate your filling out. 
Please take a few minutes to tell us about your experiences within this 
course. All data collected in this survey will be processed anonymously.


