March 26‑27, 2026
 
Webinar
 
Let Rovo Dev in Jira handle the busywork, you ship the cool stuff
 
See how Rovo Dev helps with mundane tasks such as resolving security vulnerabilities, migrations, and busy work that drains productivity.
 
What if Rovo Dev could take care of the small stuff for you – so you can stay heads‑down on the work that actually needs your brain?
 
Join our upcoming session, "Rovo Dev ships the small tasks while you tackle the cool stuff" to see how Rovo Dev turns everyday tickets into work that can move forward in the background.
 
In this talk, we''ll explore how Rovo Dev in Jira helps teams:
 
* Start and finish real dev work, like addressing  security vulnerabilities, minor bugs, and test coverage gaps, without leaving Jira
 
* Create custom prompts your team can reuse and share, and
 
* Automate away busy work
 
If your team already plans work in Jira, Rovo Dev is the fastest way to reclaim time from repetitive tasks and redirect it to the projects that really matter.
 
Save my seat
>> https://www.atlassian.com/webinars/software/ai-task-to-code?utm_source=sfmc&utm_medium=email&utm_campaign=P%3Arovo-dev%2AO%3Agdc%2AF%3Aawareness%2AC%3Awebinar%2AH%3Afy26q3%2AI%3Atask-to-code-invite-email%2AY%3Arovo-dev%2AE%3Acloud%2A&utm_sfdc-campaign_id=701QB00000ge5X4YAI_E1-ACM-10179&jobid=107921924&subid=1942065613
 
Meet the speakers
 
Matt Colman
Senior Engineering Manager

Matt Colman is a Senior Engineering Manager at Atlassian with a dynamic background spanning animation, game development, and frontend engineering. He''s led high‑impact teams at Atlassian – switching often between hands‑on IC work and strategic leadership (a proud flip‑flopper, by choice). Currently, Matt is deeply immersed in the future of AI‑driven code generation and how it can supercharge developer workflows.
 
