        (1007, null, '[]', 'Atlassian
 
Hi,
 
You trust Atlassian with some of your most business‑critical work, and we take that responsibility seriously, especially when it comes to keeping your data safe.
 
AI is already multiplying what teams can accomplish, from agents that simplify complex workflows to enterprise search and chat that quickly surface the right context when it matters.
 
With richer, more diverse customer data and usage patterns, we can deliver enhanced AI capabilities that unlock greater value across your organization. As a result, we''re updating how we use customer data so we can improve our apps and AI experiences for all customers.
 
To do this responsibly, we''re:
 
* Introducing new in‑app settings to give you full control
 
* Strengthening our existing privacy‑preserving measures with data aggregation and de‑identification
 
* Sharing information transparently throughout the process
 
These are organization‑level settings. If you manage multiple Atlassian cloud organizations, you may receive additional emails. The details below apply to the following Atlassian cloud organization(s):
 


• 2a7e168b-79cb-4348-bf66-817963584401
 


• dc405b2a-a981-4f9f-a8ec-00621a814c84
 

 

 
What is changing?
 
We''re changing Atlassian''s use of metadata and in‑app data to improve our apps and AI experiences for all customers. This change will go into effect on August 17, 2026.
>> https://support.atlassian.com/security-and-access-policies/docs/what-types-of-data-does-my-organization-contribute/?utm_source=sfmc&utm_medium=email&utm_campaign=ACM-10547&jobid=107996109&subid=1942065613

To give you control over this change, we''re introducing new in‑app settings that allow you to fully manage data contribution based on your organization''s requirements. As a valued enterprise customer, your organization has been granted the highest level of available control. Because of this, your experience may differ from what is described in our public documentation.
 
Initially, these settings will apply to data in Jira, Confluence, and Jira Service Management, including data in your Atlassian Platform apps (Rovo, Home, Teams, Projects, Assets, Goals, Analytics, and Administration). We''ll notify you when settings become available for additional apps you own, so you can review them in Atlassian Administration.
 
Between today and May 19, 2026, we''ll gradually roll out these settings in Atlassian Administration. We''ll send you another email on May 19th as a reminder, so you have time to review and make any adjustments before August 17, 2026.
 
Learn more about your available settings and how to manage them in the documentation, and review these changes in our updated legal terms, which go into effect August 17, 2026.
>> https://support.atlassian.com/security-and-access-policies/docs/manage-data-contribution-for-your-atlassian-organization/?utm_source=sfmc&utm_medium=email&utm_campaign=ACM-10547&jobid=107996109&subid=1942065613
>> https://www.atlassian.com/legal?utm_source=sfmc&utm_medium=email&utm_campaign=ACM-10547&jobid=107996109&subid=1942065613
 
Please note: this change applies to any active plan in your Atlassian organization, including trials.
 
How can you prepare?
 
To prepare for this change, we recommend that you:
 
* Understand how this change impacts you: visit our website to access centralized resources, including detailed FAQs, documentation, and register for our upcoming webinar to hear about the change from our experts.
>> https://www.atlassian.com/trust/ai/data-contribution?utm_source=sfmc&utm_medium=email&utm_campaign=ACM-10547&jobid=107996109&subid=1942065613
>> https://www.atlassian.com/webinars/enterprise-cloud/data-contribution?utm_source=sfmc&utm_medium=email&utm_campaign=ACM-10547&jobid=107996109&subid=1942065613

* Prepare your stakeholders: discuss what this change means for your organization with your security and legal teams, using our checklist for support.
>> https://dam-cdn.atl.orangelogic.com/CDNLink/AT12MW17.pdf?utm_source=sfmc&utm_medium=email&utm_campaign=ACM-10547&jobid=107996109&subid=1942065613

* Learn about data contribution settings: watch this video to see the in‑app experience today. Once your settings are available in Atlassian Administration, you can review and manage them at any time.
>> https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=-EJF6iQe4Dw
 
Our goal is to provide you with the clarity and resources you need to navigate this change confidently.
 
If you have any questions about this update and what it means for your organization, your account team is available to help you at any time.
 
Learn more
>> https://www.atlassian.com/trust/ai/data-contribution?utm_source=sfmc&utm_medium=email&utm_campaign=ACM-10547&jobid=107996109&subid=1942065613
 
Thank you,
The Atlassian team
 


