        (1076, null, '[]', 'Hey Mermaiders 👋 We know diagramming isn''t just about getting the logic right. Sometimes you want it to look pretty, too.

This month covers the full arc: say it out loud and Mermaid builds it, style it until it looks like yours (with new fonts, themes, per-node styling, and more), then sync it to wherever you already work. Here''s what''s live.
****📣 ******SAY IT: VOICE DIAGRAMMING** 
****Your diagram, out loud**
==========================**


Sometimes the fastest path from idea to diagram is just saying it. **Voice diagramming** is for the moments when you''re thinking faster than you can type, or when you want to get something on the canvas before the idea gets away. Accessible, fast, and one less reason to start from scratch. 
[ Speak it into existence ****✨****](https://f1gxg.r.a.d.sendibm1.com/mk/cl/f/sh/WCPzyXJTZ6uvcwCqTl49MOEkYcc3y6Ce/Z_oNEwfEIqFy)
******🎨**** ****STYLE IT: THEMING** 
****Woah, I didn''t know Mermaid could look like this**
====================================================**


One of our bigger update this month is **theming**, and it''s worth spending time on.


You can now save any combination of colors, fonts, and style settings as a named theme, then apply it to any diagram in one click. Build one that matches your company brand. Set up a clean editorial look for client decks. Save a code-adjacent style for architecture diagrams. 


Alongside custom themes, **four new fonts** are now available in the theming menu: *Inter, Open Sans, Merriweather, and Source Code Pro *— each one suited to a different context. Clean and modern. Editorial. Code-adjacent. Pick the one that fits the diagram, not just the one that was already there.


The theming menu itself also got a cleaner layout, with small previews for each option. Everything in one place, no more bouncing between settings.

******🎨** **STYLE IT: FONT SIZE & BOLD/ITALICS** 
****Details that make a diagram land**
====================================**


Good design is often about the small stuff. Two more updates ship this month that give you more control at the node level.


- **Bold and italics**. Bold a node''s whole label. Italicize a single word inside it. New toolbar buttons handle both – no markdown required. Works on the whole node or just the text you''ve highlighted. 
- **Font size per node**. Need a specific node to stand out, or shrink one down to fit? Set size from the toolbar (S, M, or L) on any node, without touching the code.

******🔄**** SYNC IT: CHATGPT APP & GITHUB SYNC** 
********Two new places to make your diagrams******
================================================**

[**ChatGPT Apps **→****](https://f1gxg.r.a.d.sendibm1.com/mk/cl/f/sh/WCPzyXJTZ72igyQ6pqXp88OXhPVBDnom/_P-i0Dp9W-1_)


Mermaid is now live in the ChatGPT app store. Describe what you need, get a rendered diagram back — and unlike native ChatGPT diagramming, it''s connected to your Mermaid account. Your diagrams save, sync, and stay accessible. 

[**GitHub Sync **→****](https://f1gxg.r.a.d.sendibm1.com/mk/cl/f/sh/WCPzyXJTZ7AVl0dNBw1UtsYKqCOITVQu/-vIlSw7AGrEb)

Install the Mermaid GitHub app on your repos and your diagrams stay in sync with your code automatically. When the code changes, the diagram reflects it. No manual updates, no stale architecture docs. 

****🐚** TODAY''S SEASHELLS**


- **Inviting your team got faster.** Adding people one email at a time gets old, so now you can upload a CSV and invite everyone at once. 
- **Admins can now disable public share links. **That stops diagrams from being shared via public link outside the org, so anything sensitive stays in the workspace. 
- **Finding your way around is easier now.**We separated personal and team spaces, made the search bar significantly more prominent inside folders, and cleaned up the iconography throughout. 
- **Zoom-to-cursor**** ****is live**. Canvas zoom used to anchor on the center of the viewport, so zooming in on a specific node meant extra panning to land on it. Now it anchors on your cursor. Useful when you''re editing, and especially useful when you''re walking someone else through a diagram. 
- **The**** ****shape picker**** ****got a polish pass**. Stroke weights, icon sizes, and a few design bugs have been cleaned up across flowchart shapes. 

Happy diagramming, 

*The Mermaid Team*

 

[Contact Us](https://f1gxg.r.a.d.sendibm1.com/mk/cl/f/sh/WCPzyXJTZ7vG9DuxKStXWLV5gvizzj7g/_KV1J9HtFQVy) | [Documentation](https://f1gxg.r.a.d.sendibm1.com/mk/cl/f/sh/WCPzyXJTZ833DG8DgYNDI5espic7FQjo/k4fYDruZJ2Co) | [Unsubscribe](https://f1gxg.r.a.d.sendibm1.com/mk/un/v2/sh/WCPxRrWByckTgNu6zGFOtf8n384l2A4u/YFqzuUmq3fPq)

 ', '2026-06-25 22:04:14.862264', 'Missing or invalid application ID in subject', '2026-06-02 09:01:16.000000', 'Mermaid <hello@mermaid.ai>', 'IGNORED', 'Say it. Style it. Sync it.'),
