        (1080, null, '[]', 'Dear Nguyen Pham Thu Ha (K18 HCM),


Apple opened WWDC 2026 yesterday with a rebuilt Siri and deep Apple 
Intelligence integration across iOS 27, macOS Golden Gate, and the full 
device lineup — signaling that on-device AI is now a first-tier enterprise 
and developer skill. The same week, Representatives Obernolte and Trahan 
unveiled the 269-page Great American Artificial Intelligence Act, the most 
comprehensive federal AI framework ever introduced, while EU AI Act 
high-risk provisions march toward an August enforcement date. And active 
exploits kept piling up: CISA issued emergency warnings, Cisco patched a 
zero-day SD-WAN vulnerability, and the Gartner Security & Risk Management 
Summit flagged AI-powered threats as the defining challenge of 2026. The 
skills gap is real and it is urgent.


