        (1164, null, '[]', 'July 16, 2026

Webinar

Put AI agents to work in software development

Coding agents made individual developers faster. They didn''t fix the parts of shipping software that aren''t typing: ambiguous tickets, PRs waiting on review, missing context in handoffs, stale or misaligned specs. Those still eat most of the week.

This webinar is about closing that gap. We''ll show how Jira acts as the connective tissue between agents, so the next agent (or teammate) inherits the full context, including the issue, linked specs, code repos, and documentation, instead of starting cold.

Join us on July 16, 2026 at 11 AM PT for three live workflows:

* Issue → PR, hands‑off. Assign a Jira work item to Atlassian''s coding agent (or Copilot, Cursor, or Claude). It reads the issue, the linked Confluence spec, and the codebase, then opens a PR for review.

* Oversee every agent session. Track which agents are running, which need input, and which have just opened a PR, all in Jira.

* Specs that agents can actually use. See how Jira helps define requirements and write technical specs in Confluence, ready for handoff to developers or coding agents.

We use these workflows at Atlassian. They''ve removed up to 80% of the time we''d otherwise spend on repetitive chores, like ticket triage, status updates, release notes, and more.

We''ll also share a first look at what''s next for Jira.

Save your spot
>> https://www.atlassian.com/webinars/software/agents-at-work-in-jira?utm_source=sfmc&utm_medium=email&utm_campaign=ACM-14259&jobid=108144075&subid=1942065613

