        (1179, null, '[]', 'Atlassian
 
July 16‑17, 2026
 
Webinar
 
Any agent, any model, one team
 
Most engineering teams aren''t betting on one coding agent. They''ve got Cursor in the IDE, Copilot in the repo, Claude on a laptop, and a backlog full of work that none of them have context for.
 
On July 16, we''re showing how the new Jira changes the game, giving every coding agent on your team the same shared context, and giving your team a single place to coordinate, oversee, and govern all of it.
 
In 45 minutes, you''ll see:
 
* Assign work to any agent. Whether Cursor, GitHub Copilot, and or Jira''s built‑in Jira Coding Agent, work stays grounded in Jira as the single source of truth, full context attached.
 
* One view for every agent session. Have full visibility into what agents are running, what''s blocked, and what''s ready for review, both locally and in the cloud.
 
* Spec‑driven development in Jira. The upcoming AI Planner turns PRDs, Confluence documentation, and your codebase into a structured Confluence spec, ready for a developer or coding agent to build from.
 
Inside Atlassian, 6,000 engineers already use these workflows every day. Jira Coding Agent alone now resolves 52% of our security vulnerabilities automatically, cutting cycle time in half.
 
Save your spot for the live demo and Q&A.
 
Can''t make it? Register anyway, and we''ll send you the recording.
 
Save your spot
>> https://www.atlassian.com/webinars/software/agents-at-work-in-jira?utm_source=sfmc&utm_medium=email&utm_campaign=ACM-14273&jobid=108156052&subid=1942065613
 
Meet the speakers
 
Warren Marusiak
 
Sr. Developer Evangelist, Atlassian
 
Warren is a former developer turned technical evangelist who joined Atlassian in 2021. He has worked on everything from COBOL telecoms software running on mainframes to modern cloud infrastructure at AWS. He has a passion for technology and a research background in machine learning. As a technical evangelist, Warren builds awareness of the capabilities of Atlassian products and partner integrations through demos, writings, and videos. In his spare time, you can find him practicing his passion for Brazilian Jiu‑Jitsu.
 
---------------------------------------

