        (1230, null, '[]', 'Hey Mermaiders 👋 You know the drill – you start a diagram in one place, jump somewhere else to make it look right, then dig through a repo (or six open tabs) to find it again later.


We want to keep making sure we''re closing those gaps. **Favorites right in the editor, AI that themes your diagram for you, six new diagram types, and diagrams that stay synced wherever you already work.** Here''s what''s live so you never leave your flow.
⭐**** ******FIND IT: FAVORITES** 
****Your work, one click away**
=============================**


You can now **favorite a diagram, folder, team, or presentation right from the editor** – the moment you know you''ll want it again, without a trip back to the dashboard. Favorites also has its own spot in the sidebar now, so the work you care about is always one click away. *Less hunting, more building.* 
[ Heart your next diagram ❤️](https://f1gxg.r.a.d.sendibm1.com/mk/cl/f/sh/WCPzyXJTZ72igyQ6pqXp88OXhPVBDnom/VutvAezB76s1)
******🎨********STYLE IT: AI THEMES** 
****Now AI builds the theme for you**
===================================**


Last month you could save and reuse custom themes. This month, you don''t have to build one by hand at all. Head to the **Generate** tab in the theming menu, **describe your brand or drop in your assets**, and Mermaid spins up a polished, matching theme for you (no fiddling with individual color knobs).


*On-brand without ever leaving the canvas,* no exporting to another tool just to make it look right.


[ Generate a theme ✨](https://f1gxg.r.a.d.sendibm1.com/mk/cl/f/sh/WCPzyXJTZ7AVl0dNBw1UtsYKqCOITVQu/LVNPuHzopi3F)
📐 ******MAP IT: NEW DIAGRAM TYPES** 
****Six more ways to map it out**
===============================**


**Venn, Ishikawa, Wardley, and TreeView** are now fully supported in-app – and while we were in there, we surfaced **Radar and Treemap** too. If the Mermaid syntax supports it, you should be able to work with it here – *the first place you go to play with what''s new*, no jumping to another tool to sketch a different kind of chart.


[ Try a new type ****→****](https://f1gxg.r.a.d.sendibm1.com/mk/cl/f/sh/WCPzyXJTZ7IIp2qdY1VAfci7yzHPjD32/qi4fm8pvUS8t)
******🔄**** SYNC IT: IN YOUR CODEBASE** 
********Two new ways to keep diagrams synced to code******
========================================================**

[**VS Code plugin v.2.7.0**](https://f1gxg.r.a.d.sendibm1.com/mk/cl/f/sh/WCPzyXJTZ7Q5t53tu6yqRMrv7mAWyufA/Eqg_j-3vvrHA)**[ ](https://f1gxg.r.a.d.sendibm1.com/mk/cl/f/sh/WCPzyXJTZ7Xsx7HAGCSWD71iGZ3eEcHI/_OurgiYurxgu)**[**→**](https://f1gxg.r.a.d.sendibm1.com/mk/cl/f/sh/WCPzyXJTZ7fg19UQcHwByrBVPLwlUJtQ/qYFmAehWSZsl)


Generate a Mermaid diagram straight from your source with a single CodeLens action, review changes in a side-by-side visual diff, and repair or improve a diagram – all without leaving your editor.

[**GitHub Sync **→****](https://f1gxg.r.a.d.sendibm1.com/mk/cl/f/sh/WCPzyXJTZ7nT5BhgyNPrkbLIY8psk1VY/-SEPI3wewuL3)

Install it on your repos and diagrams regenerate as your code changes – no manual redraw, no stale architecture docs.

****🐚** TODAY''S SEASHELLS**


- **Reorder your left-nav.** Drag Favorites, Teams, and the rest into whatever order works for you. 
- **One-click diagram creation.** Start a new diagram from a single button, right where you are. 
- **A faster app overall.** Snappier loads and smoother navigation, especially in diagram-heavy workspaces. 
- **Class-diagram rendering, tidied up.** Package rendering plus assorted layout fixes across the board.

Happy diagramming, 

*The Mermaid Team*

 

[Contact Us](https://f1gxg.r.a.d.sendibm1.com/mk/cl/f/sh/28xHLtxYQ509KP9MIZK4aPUsXiFGI70VT6/KAg118cU7NYT) | [Documentation](https://f1gxg.r.a.d.sendibm1.com/mk/cl/f/sh/28xHLtxYQ50fUzoV46Wh6sdSycX7s3qau8/rmqW_x7w2FD1) | [Unsubscribe](https://f1gxg.r.a.d.sendibm1.com/mk/un/v2/sh/WCPxRrWByckTgNu6zGFOtf8n384l2A4u/lyEFxf2UGXDh)

