You''re receiving this message based on your active plans, including trials, as of July 17, 2026.
 
Reminder: what is changing?
 
Atlassian is changing how we use metadata and in‑app data to improve our apps and AI experiences for all customers. With richer, more diverse customer data and usage patterns, we can build even more meaningful AI experiences that are genuinely useful in your day‑to‑day, such as more intelligent task suggestions from common assignees to recommended next steps and faster incident resolution with root cause analysis in Jira Service Management.
>> https://support.atlassian.com/security-and-access-policies/docs/what-types-of-data-does-my-organization-contribute/?utm_source=sfmc&utm_medium=email&utm_campaign=ACM-15000&jobid=108193138&subid=1942065613
 
You trust Atlassian with some of your most business‑critical work, and we take that responsibility seriously, especially when it comes to keeping your data safe. Atlassian doesn''t use metadata or in‑app data from apps that do not yet have data contribution settings available, such as Loom or Bitbucket. Before we use metadata or in‑app data from any app, we''ll provide settings so you can manage data contribution. In addition to these settings and our existing data protection safeguards, we de‑identify and aggregate contributed data before using it to improve apps for all customers.
 
How do I review my data contribution settings?
 
* To access your data contribution settings, navigate to Atlassian Administration > Security > Data contribution.
>> https://admin.atlassian.com/o/a2875916-dbc0-45df-a1f3-e051250c6d97/overview?atlOrigin=eyJpIjoiOTlhY2YzYTMtNWZjYi00ZTMwLTg5M2ItODYzZTZmM2UyMDAzIiwicCI6InNmbWMifQ

* Please note that your experience may differ from what is described in our public documentation because your organization has been granted the highest level of available control as a valued enterprise customer.
 
* For more details on how to configure your settings, the in‑scope apps they govern, and the safeguards we''re applying, please review our documentation.
>> https://support.atlassian.com/security-and-access-policies/docs/manage-data-contribution-for-your-atlassian-organization/?utm_source=sfmc&utm_medium=email&utm_campaign=ACM-15000&jobid=108193138&subid=1942065613
 
To prepare for this change, please visit our website for resources, including detailed FAQs and a change management checklist.
>> https://www.atlassian.com/trust/ai/data-contribution?utm_source=sfmc&utm_medium=email&utm_campaign=ACM-15000&jobid=108193138&subid=1942065613

>> https://www.atlassian.com/trust/ai/data-contribution/faqs?utm_source=sfmc&utm_medium=email&utm_campaign=ACM-15000&jobid=108193138&subid=1942065613

>> https://dam-cdn.atl.orangelogic.com/CDNLink/AT12MW17.pdf
 
We remain committed to providing the resources and support you need to prepare for this change.
 
