        (1281, null, '[]', 'Changelog 72 plus how a company got a 1000x latency improvement vs cold-start GIN using Lakebase Search  

Neon

--------------
Neon Changelog
--------------

We''re excited to go live with one of our most-requested features...

🎉 Project-level Permissions! ( https://neon.com/docs/changelog/2026-07-31#project-level-permissions ) 🎉

This allows you to limit access for users (and their agents) to specific projects. No access levels will change until you configure them.

This feature is rolling out progressively to existing accounts starting now. All accounts should have access by Monday.

Read the full Changelog ( https://neon.com/docs/changelog )

In case you missed it:

*
Migrating to Lakebase Search gave CommSync a 1000x, yes that''s right 1000x, latency improvement vs cold-start GIN ( https://neon.com/blog/commsync-runs-text-vector-and-hybrid-search-on-postgres-with-lakebase-search )
*
Build durable background workflows with Inngest and Neon Functions ( https://neon.com/guides/durable-workflow-on-neon-functions )
*
Build an LLM proxy with Neon Functions, Neon AI Gateway, and Managed Better Auth ( https://neon.com/guides/llm-proxy-neon-functions )
See the highlights from this week''s changelog on YouTube ( https://www.youtube.com/shorts/S5A6EYSkZAE )

