        (59, '{
  "title": "Detect N+1 Query in User Service",
  "difficulty": "EASY",
  "language": "Java",
  "problemStatement": "A junior backend team is building a simple user management module. The UserService class retrieves all users from the database and then loads each user''s roles. The current implementation executes a separate SQL query for each user to fetch their roles. Your task is to review the provided code and identify performance problems and any related security concerns. Specifically, find the N+1 query issue and suggest a more efficient approach.",
  "files": [
    {
      "filename": "src/main/java/com/example/service/UserService.java",
      "content": "package com.example.service;\\n\\nimport java.sql.*;\\nimport java.util.*;\\n\\npublic class UserService {\\n    private final Connection connection;\\n\\n    public UserService(Connection connection) {\\n        this.connection = connection;\\n    }\\n\\n    public List<User> getAllUsersWithRoles() throws SQLException {\\n        List<User> users = new ArrayList<>();\\n        String sql = \\\"SELECT id, name FROM users\\\";\\n        try (Statement stmt = connection.createStatement();\\n             ResultSet rs = stmt.executeQuery(sql)) {\\n            while (rs.next()) {\\n                int id = rs.getInt(\\\"id\\\");\\n                String name = rs.getString(\\\"name\\\");\\n                User user = new User(id, name);\\n                // N+1 query: fetch roles for each user individually\\n                String roleSql = \\\"SELECT role_name FROM user_roles WHERE user_id = \\\" + id;\\n                try (Statement roleStmt = connection.createStatement();\\n                     ResultSet roleRs = roleStmt.executeQuery(roleSql)) {\\n                    while (roleRs.next()) {\\n                        user.addRole(roleRs.getString(\\\"role_name\\\"));\\n                    }\\n                }\\n                users.add(user);\\n            }\\n        }\\n        return users;\\n    }\\n}\\n\\nclass User {\\n    private final int id;\\n    private final String name;\\n    private final List<String> roles = new ArrayList<>();\\n\\n    public User(int id, String name) {\\n        this.id = id;\\n        this.name = name;\\n    }\\n\\n    public void addRole(String role) {\\n        roles.add(role);\\n    }\\n\\n    // getters omitted for brevity\\n}",
      "language": "java"
    }
  ],
  "expectedIssues": [
    {
      "filename": "src/main/java/com/example/service/UserService.java",
      "lineNumber": 23,
      "severity": "WARNING",
      "description": "The code builds a separate SQL query for each user to fetch their roles, creating an N+1 query pattern that can severely degrade performance on large data sets. Additionally, concatenating the user id directly into the SQL string introduces a risk of SQL injection. Refactor to retrieve roles in a single query (e.g., using a JOIN or IN clause) and use a PreparedStatement with parameters."
    }
  ]
}', 2464, '2026-06-28 13:29:02.562685', 948, 'java-code-review', '6a412192fe0269a877e9dcdbbf24ec84', '{"topic":"N+1 query","difficulty":null,"targetLevel":"Junior","programmingLanguage":"Java","context":{"jobTitle":"Junior","requirement":"cơ bản","prompting":null}}', 'CODE_REVIEW_GEN', null),
        (60, '{
  "title": "Detect N+1 Query Issue in C# Class Management Service",
  "difficulty": "MEDIUM",
  "language": "C#",
  "problemStatement": "A small school management API is built using a three‑layer architecture: Controller → Service → Repository. The system stores `Class` entities, each having a collection of `Student` entities. The `ClassService.GetAllClassDtos` method builds a DTO that includes the number of students per class. However, the repository method `GetAllClasses` does not eagerly load the `Students` navigation property. When the service accesses `c.Students.Count`, Entity Framework Core issues a separate query for each class, causing an N+1 query problem. The review goal is to identify the performance flaw, explain why it is problematic, and propose a fix.",
  "files": [
    {
      "filename": "Repositories/ClassRepository.cs",
      "language": "csharp",
      "content": "using System.Collections.Generic;\\nusing System.Linq;\\nusing Microsoft.EntityFrameworkCore;\\nusing MyApp.Data;\\nusing MyApp.Models;\\n\\nnamespace MyApp.Repositories\\n{\\n    public class ClassRepository\\n    {\\n        private readonly AppDbContext _context;\\n\\n        public ClassRepository(AppDbContext context)\\n        {\\n            _context = context;\\n        }\\n\\n        public IList<Class> GetAllClasses()\\n        {\\n            // N+1 bug: Students are not eagerly loaded\\n            return _context.Classes.ToList();\\n        }\\n\\n        public Class GetClassById(int id)\\n        {\\n            return _context.Classes.FirstOrDefault(c => c.Id == id);\\n        }\\n    }\\n}\\n"
    },
    {
      "filename": "Services/ClassService.cs",
      "language": "csharp",
      "content": "using System.Collections.Generic;\\nusing MyApp.Models;\\nusing MyApp.Repositories;\\n\\nnamespace MyApp.Services\\n{\\n    public class ClassService\\n    {\\n        private readonly ClassRepository _repo;\\n\\n        public ClassService(ClassRepository repo)\\n        {\\n            _repo = repo;\\n        }\\n\\n        public IList<ClassDto> GetAllClassDtos()\\n        {\\n            var classes = _repo.GetAllClasses();\\n            var result = new List<ClassDto>();\\n            foreach (var c in classes)\\n            {\\n                var dto = new ClassDto\\n                {\\n                    Id = c.Id,\\n                    Name = c.Name,\\n                    StudentCount = c.Students.Count // triggers N+1 query\\n                };\\n                result.Add(dto);\\n            }\\n            return result;\\n        }\\n    }\\n\\n    public class ClassDto\\n    {\\n        public int Id { get; set; }\\n        public string Name { get; set; }\\n        public int StudentCount { get; set; }\\n    }\\n}\\n"
    },
    {
      "filename": "Controllers/ClassController.cs",
      "language": "csharp",
      "content": "using Microsoft.AspNetCore.Mvc;\\nusing MyApp.Services;\\n\\nnamespace MyApp.Controllers\\n{\\n    [ApiController]\\n    [Route(\"api/[controller]\")]\\n    public class ClassController : ControllerBase\\n    {\\n        private readonly ClassService _service;\\n\\n        public ClassController(ClassService service)\\n        {\\n            _service = service;\\n        }\\n\\n        [HttpGet]\\n        public IActionResult GetAll()\\n        {\\n            var dtos = _service.GetAllClassDtos();\\n            return Ok(dtos);\\n        }\\n    }\\n}\\n"
    },
    {
      "filename": "Models/Class.cs",
      "language": "csharp",
      "content": "using System.Collections.Generic;\\n\\nnamespace MyApp.Models\\n{\\n    public class Class\\n    {\\n        public int Id { get; set; }\\n        public string Name { get; set; }\\n        public IList<Student> Students { get; set; }\\n    }\\n}\\n"
    },
    {
      "filename": "Models/Student.cs",
      "language": "csharp",
      "content": "namespace MyApp.Models\\n{\\n    public class Student\\n    {\\n        public int Id { get; set; }\\n        public string FullName { get; set; }\\n        public int ClassId { get; set; }\\n    }\\n}\\n"
    },
    {
      "filename": "Data/AppDbContext.cs",
      "language": "csharp",
      "content', 3072, '2026-06-28 17:46:34.384072', 971, 'java-code-review', '6a415ded761d789d0d508632835286ce', '{"topic":"N+1 Query C#","difficulty":null,"targetLevel":"Senior","programmingLanguage":"C#","context":{"jobTitle":"Senior","requirement":"N+1 cho bài toán 1 lớp học có nhiều student, gồm 3 class controller - service -repo","prompting":null}}', 'CODE_REVIEW_GEN', null),
        (61, '{
  "title": "Detect N+1 Query in Class‑Student Retrieval",
  "difficulty": "MEDIUM",
  "language": "C#",
  "problemStatement": "You are reviewing a small ASP.NET Core service that returns a class (course) together with its enrolled students. The application follows a three‑layer architecture: Controller → Service → Repository. The repository currently loads the class entity and then queries the Students table once per student ID, causing an N+1 query problem. Your task is to identify the performance issue, explain why it is problematic, and propose a fix (e.g., using eager loading or a single join query).",
  "files": [
    {
      "filename": "Controllers/ClassController.cs",
      "language": "csharp",
      "content": "using Microsoft.AspNetCore.Mvc;\nnamespace SchoolApp.Controllers\n{\n    [ApiController]\n    [Route(\"api/[controller]\")]\n    public class ClassController : ControllerBase\n    {\n        private readonly IClassService _classService;\n        public ClassController(IClassService classService)\n        {\n            _classService = classService;\n        }\n\n        [HttpGet(\"{id}\")]\n        public IActionResult GetClass(int id)\n        {\n            var result = _classService.GetClassWithStudents(id);\n            return Ok(result);\n        }\n    }\n}"
    },
    {
      "filename": "Services/ClassService.cs",
      "language": "csharp",
      "content": "using System.Collections.Generic;\nnamespace SchoolApp.Services\n{\n    public interface IClassService\n    {\n        ClassDto GetClassWithStudents(int classId);\n    }\n\n    public class ClassService : IClassService\n    {\n        private readonly IClassRepository _classRepository;\n        public ClassService(IClassRepository classRepository)\n        {\n            _classRepository = classRepository;\n        }\n\n        public ClassDto GetClassWithStudents(int classId)\n        {\n            return _classRepository.FetchClassWithStudents(classId);\n        }\n    }\n}"
    },
    {
      "filename": "Repositories/ClassRepository.cs",
      "language": "csharp",
      "content": "using System.Collections.Generic;\nusing System.Linq;\nusing Microsoft.EntityFrameworkCore;\nnamespace SchoolApp.Repositories\n{\n    public interface IClassRepository\n    {\n        ClassDto FetchClassWithStudents(int classId);\n    }\n\n    public class ClassRepository : IClassRepository\n    {\n        private readonly SchoolContext _context;\n        public ClassRepository(SchoolContext context)\n        {\n            _context = context;\n        }\n\n        public ClassDto FetchClassWithStudents(int classId)\n        {\n            var classEntity = _context.Classes\n                .FirstOrDefault(c => c.Id == classId);\n            if (classEntity == null) return null;\n\n            var studentDtos = new List<StudentDto>();\n            foreach (var studentId in classEntity.StudentIds)\n            {\n                var student = _context.Students\n                    .FirstOrDefault(s => s.Id == studentId); // N+1 query\n                if (student != null)\n                {\n                    studentDtos.Add(new StudentDto\n                    {\n                        Id = student.Id,\n                        Name = student.Name\n                    });\n                }\n            }\n\n            return new ClassDto\n            {\n                Id = classEntity.Id,\n                Name = classEntity.Name,\n                Students = studentDtos\n            };\n        }\n    }\n}"
    }
  ],
  "expectedIssues": [
    {
      "filename": "Repositories/ClassRepository.cs",
      "lineNumber": 29,
      "severity": "WARNING",
      "description": "The line performs a separate query for each student ID, resulting in an N+1 query pattern. This causes many round‑trips to the database and degrades performance, especially for classes with many students. Fix by loading students in a single query (e.g., use Include(e => e.Students) or a join) or by retrieving all needed student records with a single WHERE IN clause."
    }
  ]
}', 2406, '2026-06-28 17:46:56.290004', 971, 'java-code-review', '6a415e056f6972905994e8c489a06802', '{"topic":"N+1 Query C#","difficulty":null,"targetLevel":"Intern","programmingLanguage":"C#","context":{"jobTitle":"Intern","requirement":"N+1 cho bài toán 1 lớp học có nhiều student, gồm 3 class controller - service -repo","prompting":null}}', 'CODE_REVIEW_GEN', null),
        (62, '{
  "title": "Detect N+1 Query Issue in Classroom Service",
  "difficulty": "MEDIUM",
  "language": "Java",
  "problemStatement": "A small Spring Boot application manages classroom information. The controller exposes an endpoint to retrieve a class together with its enrolled students. The service layer currently loads the class entity and then, for each student ID, queries the repository for the student details. This pattern can cause an N+1 query problem, leading to severe performance degradation when a class has many students. Your task as the reviewer is to identify the N+1 issue, explain why it is problematic, and propose a fix that retrieves all students in a single query.",
  "files": [
    {
      "filename": "src/main/java/com/example/controller/ClassController.java",
      "language": "java",
      "content": "package com.example.controller;\n\nimport org.springframework.web.bind.annotation.*;\nimport com.example.service.ClassService;\nimport com.example.dto.ClassDto;\nimport java.util.List;\n\n@RestController\n@RequestMapping(\"/classes\")\npublic class ClassController {\n\n    private final ClassService classService;\n\n    public ClassController(ClassService classService) {\n        this.classService = classService;\n    }\n\n    @GetMapping(\"/{id}\")\n    public ClassDto getClass(@PathVariable Long id) {\n        return classService.getClassWithStudents(id);\n    }\n}\n"
    },
    {
      "filename": "src/main/java/com/example/service/ClassService.java",
      "language": "java",
      "content": "package com.example.service;\n\nimport com.example.repo.ClassRepository;\nimport com.example.dto.ClassDto;\nimport com.example.dto.StudentDto;\nimport com.example.entity.ClassEntity;\nimport com.example.entity.StudentEntity;\nimport org.springframework.stereotype.Service;\nimport java.util.List;\nimport java.util.stream.Collectors;\n\n@Service\npublic class ClassService {\n\n    private final ClassRepository classRepository;\n\n    public ClassService(ClassRepository classRepository) {\n        this.classRepository = classRepository;\n    }\n\n    public ClassDto getClassWithStudents(Long classId) {\n        ClassEntity classEntity = classRepository.findById(classId);\n        // N+1 problem: fetching each student individually\n        List<StudentDto> students = classEntity.getStudentIds().stream()\n            .map(id -> {\n                StudentEntity student = classRepository.findStudentById(id);\n                return new StudentDto(student.getId(), student.getName());\n            })\n            .collect(Collectors.toList());\n\n        return new ClassDto(classEntity.getId(), classEntity.getName(), students);\n    }\n}\n"
    },
    {
      "filename": "src/main/java/com/example/repo/ClassRepository.java",
      "language": "java",
      "content": "package com.example.repo;\n\nimport com.example.entity.ClassEntity;\nimport com.example.entity.StudentEntity;\nimport org.springframework.stereotype.Repository;\nimport javax.persistence.*;\nimport java.util.List;\n\n@Repository\npublic class ClassRepository {\n\n    @PersistenceContext\n    private EntityManager em;\n\n    public ClassEntity findById(Long id) {\n        return em.find(ClassEntity.class, id);\n    }\n\n    public StudentEntity findStudentById(Long id) {\n        return em.find(StudentEntity.class, id);\n    }\n\n    // Incorrect: should fetch all students in one query\n    public List<StudentEntity> findStudentsByClassId(Long classId) {\n        String jpql = \"SELECT s FROM StudentEntity s WHERE s.classId = :classId\";\n        return em.createQuery(jpql, StudentEntity.class)\n                 .setParameter(\"classId\", classId)\n                 .getResultList();\n    }\n}\n"
    }
  ],
  "expectedIssues": [
    {
      "filename": "src/main/java/com/example/service/ClassService.java",
      "lineNumber": 26,
      "severity": "CRITICAL",
      "description": "The service fetches each student with a separate call to classRepository.findStudentById inside the stream, causing an N+1 query problem. For a class with many students this results in many database round‑trips and poor performance. Replace the per‑student lookup with a single call to classRepository.findStudentsByClassId(classId) and map the returned list to StudentDto objects."
    }
  ]
}', 2764, '2026-06-28 17:52:35.739320', 967, 'java-code-review', '6a415f59ebd72a3f36e4eb048e0bae84', '{"topic":"N+1","difficulty":null,"targetLevel":"Senior","programmingLanguage":"Java","context":{"jobTitle":"Senior","requirement":"N+1 cho bài toán 1 lớp học có nhiều sutdent, 3 file controller - service - repo","prompting":null}}', 'CODE_REVIEW_GEN', null),
        (63, '{
  "questionText": "Consider a Spring-based application that utilizes Java Core principles and Object-Oriented Programming (OOP) concepts. Suppose you have a class `UserService` that depends on another class `UserRepository` for database operations. The `UserRepository` class is annotated with `@Repository` and implements the `CrudRepository` interface. However, due to a recent requirement change, you need to introduce an aspect that logs every method call to `UserRepository`. You decide to use Spring''s Aspect-Oriented Programming (AOP) feature to achieve this. \\n\\nGiven the following code snippet: \\n```java\\n\\n@Aspect\\npublic class LoggingAspect {\\n\\n    @Before(\"execution(* *(..))\")\\n    public void logBefore(JoinPoint joinPoint) {\\n        System.out.println(\"Before: \" + joinPoint.getSignature().getName());\\n    }\\n\\n    @After(\"execution(* *(..))\")\\n    public void logAfter(JoinPoint joinPoint) {\\n        System.out.println(\"After: \" + joinPoint.getSignature().getName());\\n    }\\n}\\n```\\n\\nWhat would be the most suitable advice type to introduce a logging functionality that logs every method call to `UserRepository` without affecting the original method''s execution, and why?\\n",
  "options": [
    "A. Use `@Around` advice to log method calls, as it allows for the execution of the original method.",
    "B. Use `@Before` advice to log method calls, as it executes before the original method and does not affect its execution.",
    "C. Use `@After` advice to log method calls, as it executes after the original method and does not affect its execution.",
    "D. Use `@AfterReturning` and `@AfterThrowing` advice to log method calls, as they provide more fine-grained control over logging."
  ],
  "correctAnswer": "A"
}', 425, '2026-06-30 06:22:29.220179', 690, 'java', '6a43609c30ef11fd749229d3c787bff5', '{"categoryName":"Java","difficulty":"HARD","topics":["Spring","OOP","Java Core"],"additionalPrompt":"Focus on deep understanding"}', 'QUIZ_GEN', null),
