findByUserId(user.getId()) inside a loop over all users, causing one additional query per user (N+1 query problem). This results in many unnecessary round‑trips to the database and degrades performance. Fix by fetching orders for all users in a single query (e.g., using a JOIN FETCH, @EntityGraph, or a batch query) and then grouping them by user ID."}]},"submissions":[{"filename":"src/main/java/com/example/service/UserOrderService.java","lineNumber":31,"severity":"WARNING","description":"Potential N+1 query issue. orderRepository.findByUserId(user.getId()) is executed inside a loop, causing one database query per user. This can lead to significant performance degradation when processing many users. Consider fetching all orders in a single query using JOIN FETCH, EntityGraph, or batch loading."},{"filename":"src/main/java/com/example/dto/UserDto.java","lineNumber":8,"severity":"CRITICAL","description":"The password field is included in the DTO without @JsonIgnore, causing credentials to be serialized and sent to clients. This leaks sensitive information. Fix by adding @JsonIgnore to the password field or removing it from the response model.\n"},{"filename":"src/main/java/com/example/dto/UserDto.java","lineNumber":16,"severity":"CRITICAL","description":"Security configuration uses anyRequest().permitAll(), which disables authentication and authorization for all endpoints, exposing the API to unauthenticated access. Restrict access by defining proper antMatchers and requiring authentication."}]}', 'CODE_REVIEW', null),
