        (170, '{"score": 75, "extraMetrics": {"Subject Line Quality": {"score": 1, "maxScore": 10, "comment": "The subject line ''[INBLUE-APP-107]'' is an internal reference code and provides no context about the email''s purpose (e.g., interview confirmation, candidate''s name, position), making it uninformative for the recipient."}, "Salutation And Opening": {"score": 9, "maxScore": 10, "comment": "The salutation ''Dear HR Team at FBT Software,'' is appropriate and professional. The opening is clear, polite, and expresses enthusiasm for the interview opportunity for an intern position."}, "Content And Clarity": {"score": 25, "maxScore": 25, "comment": "The content is exceptionally clear and purposeful. It confirms availability, demonstrates preparation by referencing the internship description, and proactively asks for further information. It perfectly addresses the scenario of confirming an interview for an intern role."}, "Tone And Professionalism": {"score": 10, "maxScore": 20, "comment": "The tone is professional, polite, and enthusiastic throughout the email. However, there is a critical mismatch between the sender''s name in the email address (''Tran Nhat Tan'') and the name in the signature (''Tran Binh An''), which is a significant professional oversight."}, "Grammar And Vocabulary": {"score": 20, "maxScore": 20, "comment": "The email is grammatically flawless and uses appropriate, professional vocabulary. There are no spelling errors or awkward phrasing."}, "Closing And Signature": {"score": 5, "maxScore": 10, "comment": "The closing ''Best regards,'' is appropriate, but the signature ''Tran Binh An'' contradicts the sender''s name in the email address, which is a major professional inconsistency."}, "Formatting And Structure": {"score": 5, "maxScore": 5, "comment": "The email is very well-structured with clear paragraphs, enhancing readability and professional presentation."}, "Strength": ["Clear, concise, and purposeful content, effectively confirming interview availability and demonstrating preparedness for an intern role.", "Professional, polite, and enthusiastic tone within the message.", "Excellent grammar, spelling, and appropriate vocabulary.", "Well-structured and easy to read."], "Weakness": ["Critical mismatch between the sender''s name in the email address and the name provided in the signature.", "Uninformative subject line, which could lead to the email being overlooked or misfiled."], "General Comment": "This email is well-written and effectively conveys its message, demonstrating strong communication skills. However, the significant inconsistency between the sender''s name and the signature, along with the uninformative subject line, are critical professional oversights that must be addressed, especially for an intern application where attention to detail is key."}}', 601, '2026-07-28 17:28:47.533151', 23723, 'java-backend', 'no-trace-id', '{"emailContext":{"scenario":"","level":"INTERN","candidateEmail":{"senderEmail":"\"(K18 HCM), Tran Nhat Tan\" <tantnse184055@fpt.edu.vn>","subject":"[INBLUE-APP-107]","bodyText":"Dear HR Team at FBT Software,\r\n\r\nThank you very much for getting back to me and for the opportunity to\r\ninterview for the Java Backend Intern position. I am thrilled to move\r\nforward in the recruitment process.\r\n\r\nI would like to confirm my availability for the upcoming interview sessions\r\nas outlined in your previous communication. I have thoroughly reviewed the\r\ninternship description, and I am eager to discuss how my academic\r\nbackground and eagerness to learn align with FBT Software''s goals.\r\n\r\nPlease let me know if you need any further information or additional\r\ndocuments from my side before the interview.\r\n\r\nThank you again for your time and consideration. I look forward to speaking\r\nwith the team soon.\r\n\r\nBest regards,\r\nTran Binh An","attachmentUrls":"[]"}},"evaluationCriteria":{"maxScore":100,"aiSystemPrompt":"","extraMetrics":["Closing And Signature","Formatting And Structure","Content And Clarity","Grammar And Vocabulary","General Comment","Salutation And Opening","Strength","Subject Line Quality","Tone And Professionalism","Weakness"]}}', 'EMAIL', null),
        (126, '{
  "score": 50,
  "extraMetrics": {
    "Bug Detection": 5,
    "Security Awareness": 4,
    "Performance Analysis": 5,
    "Code Smell Detection": 5,
    "Solution Quality": 4,
    "Clean Code Awareness": 5,
    "Missed Issues": "Ứng viên xác định sai vị trí dòng code của lỗi bảo mật trong SecurityConfig (chỉ ra dòng 16 của UserDto thay vì SecurityConfig.java). Ngoài ra, ứng viên đánh giá sai mức độ nghiêm trọng (Severity) của cả hai lỗi, coi đây là WARNING thay vì CRITICAL, cho thấy sự thiếu hụt kiến thức về tác động của việc lộ thông tin nhạy cảm và lỗ hổng xác thực.",
    "Strength": "Ứng viên có khả năng nhận diện được các vấn đề logic cơ bản trong code và chỉ ra được các điểm cần cải thiện về mặt chức năng.",
    "Weakness": "Thiếu tư duy bảo mật (Security Mindset) nghiêm trọng. Việc đánh giá các lỗ hổng rò rỉ thông tin xác thực và mất kiểm soát truy cập là ''WARNING'' cho thấy ứng viên chưa hiểu rõ rủi ro thực tế trong môi trường sản xuất.",
    "General Comment": "Ứng viên cần cải thiện kỹ năng đánh giá mức độ nghiêm trọng của các lỗ hổng bảo mật. Việc nhầm lẫn file và dòng code cho thấy sự thiếu cẩn trọng trong quá trình review. Cần học hỏi thêm về OWASP Top 10 và các tiêu chuẩn bảo mật trong Spring Security."
  }
}', 348, '2026-07-21 08:04:48.178138', 1915, 'java-backend89', '6a5f2818ae9b28faaab78ad17ae2ec4d', '{"evaluationCriteria":{"maxScore":100,"aiSystemPrompt":"","extraMetrics":["Bug Detection","Security Awareness","Performance Analysis","Code Smell Detection","Solution Quality","Clean Code Awareness","Strength","Weakness","General Comment","Missed Issues"]},"codeReviewProblem":{"title":"Sensitive Information Leakage via API","difficulty":"HARD","language":"Java","problemStatement":"A small Spring Boot style service exposes a REST endpoint that returns a list of users. The project consists of four source files: UserController.java, UserService.java, UserDto.java, and SecurityConfig.java. The code contains two critical security flaws: (1) the UserDto includes the password field in JSON responses, leaking credentials; (2) the security configuration permits all requests without authentication. The candidate must review the code, identify the exact locations of these issues, assess their severity, and propose proper fixes (e.g., adding @JsonIgnore to the password field and restricting endpoint access).","files":[{"filename":"src/main/java/com/example/dto/UserDto.java","content":"package com.example.dto;\n\nimport com.fasterxml.jackson.annotation.JsonIgnore;\n\npublic class UserDto {\n    private Long id;\n    private String username;\n    private String password; // BUG: password should be ignored in JSON responses\n    private String email;\n\n    public Long getId() { return id; }\n    public void setId(Long id) { this.id = id; }\n\n    public String getUsername() { return username; }\n    public void setUsername(String username) { this.username = username; }\n\n    public String getPassword() { return password; }\n    public void setPassword(String password) { this.password = password; }\n\n    public String getEmail() { return email; }\n    public void setEmail(String email) { this.email = email; }\n}\n","language":"java"},{"filename":"src/main/java/com/example/service/UserService.java","content":"package com.example.service;\n\nimport com.example.dto.UserDto;\nimport java.util.ArrayList;\nimport java.util.List;\n\npublic class UserService {\n    public List<UserDto> getAllUsers() {\n        // In a real app this would query a DB\n        List<UserDto> users = new ArrayList<>();\n        UserDto u = new UserDto();\n        u.setId(1L);\n        u.setUsername(\"alice\");\n        u.setPassword(\"secret123\"); // password stored in plain text\n        u.setEmail(\"alice@example.com\");\n        users.add(u);\n        return users;\n    }\n}\n","language":"java"},{"filename":"src/main/java/com/example/controller/UserController.java","content":"package com.example.controller;\n\nimport com.example.dto.UserDto;\nimport com.example.service.UserService;\nimport org.springframework.web.bind.annotation.GetMapping;\nimport org.springframework.web.bind.annotation.RestController;\nimport java.util.List;\n\n@RestController\npublic class UserController {\n    private final UserService userService = new UserService();\n\n    @GetMapping(\"/users\")\n    public List<UserDto> listUsers() {\n        return userService.getAllUsers();\n    }\n}\n","language":"java"},{"filename":"src/main/java/com/example/config/SecurityConfig.java","content":"package com.example.config;\n\nimport org.springframework.context.annotation.Configuration;\nimport org.springframework.security.config.annotation.web.builders.HttpSecurity;\nimport org.springframework.security.config.annotation.web.configuration.EnableWebSecurity;\nimport org.springframework.security.config.annotation.web.configuration.WebSecurityConfigurerAdapter;\n\n@Configuration\n@EnableWebSecurity\npublic class SecurityConfig extends WebSecurityConfigurerAdapter {\n    @Override\n    protected void configure(HttpSecurity http) throws Exception {\n        http\n            .csrf().disable()\n            .authorizeRequests()\n                .anyRequest().permitAll(); // BUG: all endpoints are publicly accessible\n    }\n}\n","language":"java"}],"expectedIssues":[{"filename":"src/main/java/com/example/dto/UserDto.java","lineNumber":8,"severity":"CRITICAL","description":"The password field is included in the DTO without @JsonIgnore, causing credentials to be serialized and sent to clients. This leaks sensitive information. Fix by adding @JsonIgnore to the password field or removing it from the response model."},{"filename":"src/main/java/com/example/config/SecurityConfig.java","lineNumber":16,"severity":"CRITICAL","description":"Security configuration uses anyRequest().permitAll(), which disables authentication and authorization for all endpoints, exposing the API to unauthenticated access. Restrict access by defining proper antMatchers and requiring authentication."}]},"submissions":[{"filename":"src/main/java/com/example/dto/UserDto.java","lineNumber":8,"severity":"WARNING","description":"password should be ignored in JSON responses"},{"filename":"src/main/java/com/example/dto/UserDto.java","lineNumber":16,"severity":"WARNING","description":"all endpoints are publicly accessible"}]}', 'CODE_REVIEW', null),
