  "options": [
    "A. To provide a framework for building command-line interfaces",
    "B. To handle HTTP requests and responses in a structured manner",
    "C. To interact with databases using SQL queries",
    "D. To create desktop applications with a graphical user interface"
  ],
  "correctAnswer": "B"
}', 158, '2026-07-29 13:03:46.207485', 684, 'java', '6a69fa2b11a7f041d2dddb13240184fa', '{"categoryName":null,"difficulty":"MEDIUM","topics":["NodeJS"],"additionalPrompt":"Bussiness"}', 'QUIZ_GEN', null),
        (185, '{
  "title": "Review Customer Order Retrieval Procedure",
  "difficulty": "EASY",
  "language": "SQL",
  "problemStatement": "The company provides a stored procedure GetCustomerOrders that returns all orders for a given customer. Business rule: only authorized internal services should call this procedure, and it must safely handle the CustomerId input. The code currently builds a dynamic SQL string by concatenating the input parameter. Your task is to review the provided SQL script and identify security flaws, specifically SQL injection vulnerabilities, and suggest a proper fix using parameterized queries.",
  "files": [
    {
      "filename": "scripts/GetCustomerOrders.sql",
