ioned, severely undermines the candidate''s attention to detail and the overall effectiveness of the communication. | Content And Clarity: {score=10, comment=The content clearly articulates the candidate''s understanding of the feedback regarding the UI/UX mismatch and proactively proposes alternative roles (Fresher Front-end/Back-end/Java Developer) that align with their actual skills. It highlights relevant strengths for these roles. However, the email explicitly states ''Em có đính kèm lại CV định hướng Lập trình viên trong email này'' (I have attached the Programmer-oriented CV in this email), but no attachment was actually included, which is a critical failure., maxScore=25}; Subject Line Quality: {score=1, comment=The subject line ''[INBLUE-APP-133]'' is an internal reference code and fails to provide context about the email''s purpose, making it uninformative for the recipient., maxScore=10}; Closing And Signature: {score=7, comment=The closing is polite and appreciative. The signature includes the candidate''s name and phone number, which is adequate, but it implicitly references a missing attachment., maxScore=10}; Grammar And Vocabulary: {score=20, comment=Assuming the Vietnamese is correct, the email is grammatically flawless and uses appropriate, professional vocabulary throughout. There are no spelling errors or awkward phrasing., maxScore=20}; Salutation And Opening: {score=9, comment=The salutation ''Kính gửi Anh/Chị,'' is polite. The opening effectively acknowledges and thanks for the previous feedback, setting a positive and receptive tone., maxScore=10}; Formatting And Structure: {score=5, comment=The email is very well-structured with clear paragraphs, enhancing readability and professional presentation., maxScore=5}; Tone And Professionalism: {score=12, comment=The tone is highly professional, humble, and proactive, demonstrating a strong ability to receive and act on feedback positively. However, the absence of the promised attachment significan