.findByUserId(user.getId()) inside a loop over all users, causing one additional query per user (N+1 query problem). This results in many unnecessary round‑trips to the database and degrades performance. Fix by fetching orders for all users in a single query (e.g., using a JOIN FETCH, @EntityGraph, or a batch query) and then grouping them by user ID."}]},"submissions":[{"filename":"src/main/java/com/example/service/UserOrderService.java","lineNumber":31,"severity":"CRITICAL","description":"N+1 Query Problem"},{"filename":"src/main/java/com/example/service/UserOrderService.java","lineNumber":29,"severity":"WARNING","description":"Dùng Entity User làm Key trong Map"},{"filename":"src/main/java/com/example/service/UserOrderService.java","lineNumber":27,"severity":"WARNING","description":"Vấn đề Out of Memory (OOM)"}]}', 'CODE_REVIEW', 15.99),
